    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0875" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1423: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-10T14:00:00-04:00">October 10, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>103. Your telegram 41, October 9, 6 p.m., and my telegram 102, October 10, 11
                        a.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d620-f1"/> By Presidential decree Soler and
                    Vasconcellos in the quality of plenipotentiaries on special mission and Ynsfran
                    in the quality of Counselor are constituted Paraguay’s commission to study the
                    pact of nonaggression.</p>
                <pb facs="0876" n="762" xml:id="pg762"/>
                <p>The reply to the Legation’s note presented pursuant to the Department’s telegram
                    40, October 3, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d620-f2"/> has just been handed me.
                    Omitting opening and closing salutation it reads as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to state to Your Excellency that my Government sometime
                            since ordered the national troops to refrain from committing acts of
                            provocation, these orders having been repeated on this occasion. The
                            encounters to which the note of Your Excellency refers have not occurred
                            through causes chargeable to the army of my country, they being due to
                            the frequent incursions or advances made by Bolivian forces in the
                            direction of Paraguayan fortins.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
